{"arrivo":"pt","origine":"la","origine_nome":"Latin","livello2":"roa-opt","livello2_nome":"Old Galician-Portuguese","n":5,"parole":[{"parola":"a eito","pos":"adv","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"uninterruptedly, without intermission or interruption","termine_origine":"ad","catena":[{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"ad","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"roa-opt","nome":"Old Galician-Portuguese","termine":"a eito","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"roa-opt","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From a (from Latin ad) + eito (from Latin ictus). From Old Galician-Portuguese a eito. Cognate with Galician a eito."},{"parola":"adoração","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"latinismo_dotto","incerta":"no","significato":"adoration","termine_origine":"adoratio","catena":[{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"adoratio","categoria":"latinismo_dotto"},{"codice":"roa-opt","nome":"Old Galician-Portuguese","termine":"aoraçon","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"roa-opt","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Learned borrowing from Latin adōrātiōnem. By surface analysis, adorar + -ção. Displaced Old Galician-Portuguese aoraçon."},{"parola":"aspecto","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"latinismo_dotto","incerta":"no","significato":"appearance, look","termine_origine":"aspectus","catena":[{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"aspectus","categoria":"latinismo_dotto"},{"codice":"roa-opt","nome":"Old Galician-Portuguese","termine":"aspeito","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"roa-opt","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Learned borrowing from Latin aspectus; displaced aspeito, from Old Galician-Portuguese aspeito."},{"parola":"calcanhar","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"heel (part of the foot)","termine_origine":"calcāneum","catena":[{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"calcāneum","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"roa-opt","nome":"Old Galician-Portuguese","termine":"","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"roa-opt","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"From the now uncommon and mostly slang term calcanho (“foot; heel”), itself from Latin calcāneum (“heel”) (whence also the learned borrowing calcâneo), from Latin calx; less likely from a Vulgar Latin *calcaneāre. Appears as calcannar in Old Galician-Portuguese. Compare Spanish calcañar."},{"parola":"sombra","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Of uncertain origin; Possibly; modello unc/uncertain","significato":"shadow","termine_origine":"umbra","catena":[{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"umbra","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"roa-opt","nome":"Old Galician-Portuguese","termine":"soombrar","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"la-vul","nome":"Vulgar Latin","termine":"*subumbrō","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"osp","nome":"Old Spanish","termine":"solombra","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-vul","nome":"Vulgar Latin","termine":"*solumbra","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"roa-opt","nome":"Old Galician-Portuguese","termine":"sol","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"roa-opt","ambiti":["arte"],"via":"","testo":"From Old Galician-Portuguese soombra, of uncertain origin, but ultimately containing Latin umbra (“shadow”). Possible etymologies include: * from Old Galician-Portuguese soombrar, from Vulgar Latin *subumbrāre (“to shadow”), from Latin sub + umbrāre, from umbra (“shadow”). * from Old Spanish solombr"}]}